      "side": 1,
      "message": "Soong is strict on dependencies: if you add a library as a dependency, then the library must also be known by Soong. I.e., you cannot add a library defined in \"Android.mk\" as a dependency of an app defined in \"Android.bp\". Therefore, the case that you are worrying about doesn\u0027t exist.\n\nOn the contrary, Make is more lenient on dependencies: you can add anything to LOCAL_OPTIONAL_USES_LIBRARIES, no matter the libraries are built by Make or Soong, or even nobody. If nobody builds the libraries, the build will fail at the Ninja phase.",
      "parentUuid": "d67cb7a9_eb8ac170",
      "range": {
